model_response:
The fast‑lane car travels at  

\[
v_{\text{fast}} = 60\ \text{mi/h}
\]

The slow‑lane car travels at half that speed:

\[
v_{\text{slow}} = \frac{1}{2}\,v_{\text{fast}} = \frac{1}{2}\times 60 = 30\ \text{mi/h}
\]

Both cars need to cover the same distance of  

\[
d = 480\ \text{mi}
\]

The time required is distance divided by speed:

\[
t_{\text{slow}} = \frac{d}{v_{\text{slow}}}
               = \frac{480\ \text{mi}}{30\ \text{mi/h}}
               = 16\ \text{hours}
\]

\[
\boxed{16\ \text{hours}}
\]
